  "acenocoumarol plus aceclofenac: NSAID-induced platelet inhibition and GI mucosal injury add to anticoagulation; GI/serious bleeding risk multiplies. Management: avoid NSAIDs entirely; use paracetamol for pain; if unavoidable, shortest course with PPI cover and INR checks.",
  "DDInter 2.0 coverage pattern (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0); mechanism/management authored from label-level pharmacology",
  "acenocoumarol plus aspirin combines anticoagulation with antiplatelet effect; major bleeding risk is roughly doubled. Management: only under explicit direction (e.g. ACS, mechanical valve), keep INR 2.0-2.5, GI protection with PPI, briefest possible overlap, educate on bleeding signs and never stop either drug on their own.",
