  "Both azithromycin (macrolide antibiotic) and venlafaxine (antidepressant) prolong cardiac repolarization via IKr (hERG) channel blockade; additive QTc prolongation and torsades-de-pointes risk, higher with hypokalemia, bradycardia, female sex or structural heart disease. Management: baseline ECG with QTc before co-prescription, correct potassium/magnesium, prefer non-QT alternatives; avoid in known long-QT syndrome.",
  "Both azithromycin (macrolide antibiotic) and voriconazole (azole antifungal) prolong cardiac repolarization via IKr (hERG) channel blockade; additive QTc prolongation and torsades-de-pointes risk, higher with hypokalemia, bradycardia, female sex or structural heart disease. Management: baseline ECG with QTc before co-prescription, correct potassium/magnesium, prefer non-QT alternatives; avoid in known long-QT syndrome.",
