  "esomeprazole raises gastric pH and abolishes atazanavir absorption (needs acid); treatment failure and resistance. Management: switch the PPI to famotidine or an atazanavir/ritonavir boosted regimen per HIV guidance.",
  "esomeprazole inhibits CYP2C19, reducing clopidogrel activation to its active metabolite; antiplatelet effect can fall. Management: prefer pantoprazole for gastroprotection; the clinical signal is small but switch is low-cost. Never stop clopidogrel post-stent over this.",
  "itraconazole capsules need gastric acid; esomeprazole reduces absorption. Management: give itraconazole with an acidic drink (cola) or switch to solution/alternative antifungal.",
  "esomeprazole reduces levothyroxine absorption (chelation or acid-dependent dissolution); hypothyroid drift over weeks. Management: take levothyroxine fasting and separate esomeprazole by at least 4 hours; recheck TSH 6-8 weeks after any change.",
