  "lansoprazole raises gastric pH and abolishes atazanavir absorption (needs acid); treatment failure and resistance. Management: switch the PPI to famotidine or an atazanavir/ritonavir boosted regimen per HIV guidance.",
  "itraconazole capsules need gastric acid; lansoprazole reduces absorption. Management: give itraconazole with an acidic drink (cola) or switch to solution/alternative antifungal.",
  "lansoprazole reduces levothyroxine absorption (chelation or acid-dependent dissolution); hypothyroid drift over weeks. Management: take levothyroxine fasting and separate lansoprazole by at least 4 hours; recheck TSH 6-8 weeks after any change.",
  "Leflunomide can potentiate warfarin and hepatotoxicity. Management: INR and LFT checks in the first month of co-use.",
  "levofloxacin plus betamethasone: increased tendon-rupture risk, especially the elderly and on steroid therapy. Management: warn on sudden heel/shoulder pain and rest immediately; prefer non-FQ antibiotics if long steroid courses are planned.",
