  "lisinopril plus chlorthalidone is a standard BP/HF combination but can over-drop BP and worsen renal perfusion with volume loss. Management: titrate gradually, check standing BP, creatinine and K+ (opposite-direction effects) after initiation.",
  "Trimethoprim (in cotrimoxazole) acts like an amiloride; with lisinopril life-threatening hyperkalemia can develop within days, especially in the elderly or CKD. Management: prefer an alternative antibiotic; if used, check K+ in 3-5 days, avoid in eGFR < 30.",
