  "ketoprofen blunts olmesartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
  "olmesartan lowers lithium clearance (renal), raising levels toward toxicity. Management: check lithium level 7-10 days after start/dose change, watch tremor, GI upset, confusion; adjust dose.",
  "mefenamic acid blunts olmesartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
