  "piroxicam blunts olmesartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
  "olmesartan plus spironolactone both raise serum potassium (reduced aldosterone effect plus potassium excretion block); hyperkalemia risk, dangerous with renal impairment or diabetes. Management: check K+ and creatinine at 1-2 weeks and after dose changes, avoid other K-raising drugs, salt substitutes off, hold if K+ > 5.5.",
  "tolfenamic acid blunts olmesartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
  "olmesartan plus torasemide is a standard BP/HF combination but can over-drop BP and worsen renal perfusion with volume loss. Management: titrate gradually, check standing BP, creatinine and K+ (opposite-direction effects) after initiation.",
  "omeprazole raises gastric pH and abolishes atazanavir absorption (needs acid); treatment failure and resistance. Management: switch the PPI to famotidine or an atazanavir/ritonavir boosted regimen per HIV guidance.",
  "omeprazole inhibits CYP2C19, reducing clopidogrel activation to its active metabolite; antiplatelet effect can fall. Management: prefer pantoprazole for gastroprotection; the clinical signal is small but switch is low-cost. Never stop clopidogrel post-stent over this.",
  "itraconazole capsules need gastric acid; omeprazole reduces absorption. Management: give itraconazole with an acidic drink (cola) or switch to solution/alternative antifungal.",
  "omeprazole reduces levothyroxine absorption (chelation or acid-dependent dissolution); hypothyroid drift over weeks. Management: take levothyroxine fasting and separate omeprazole by at least 4 hours; recheck TSH 6-8 weeks after any change.",
