  "rabeprazole raises gastric pH and abolishes atazanavir absorption (needs acid); treatment failure and resistance. Management: switch the PPI to famotidine or an atazanavir/ritonavir boosted regimen per HIV guidance.",
  "itraconazole capsules need gastric acid; rabeprazole reduces absorption. Management: give itraconazole with an acidic drink (cola) or switch to solution/alternative antifungal.",
  "rabeprazole reduces levothyroxine absorption (chelation or acid-dependent dissolution); hypothyroid drift over weeks. Management: take levothyroxine fasting and separate rabeprazole by at least 4 hours; recheck TSH 6-8 weeks after any change.",
