  "roxithromycin raises warfarin exposure/INR (CYP3A4 for clarithromycin/erythromycin; gut-flora and P-gp effects for azithromycin); bleeding risk. Management: INR check 3-5 days after starting the antibiotic, watch for bruising; azithromycin is the preferred macrolide if warfarin cannot be held.",
  "roxithromycin slows theophylline clearance; nausea and tachyarrhythmia risk. Management: monitor level or reduce dose ~30% during the antibiotic course.",
  "aceclofenac blunts sacubitril+valsartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
  "aspirin blunts sacubitril+valsartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
