  "sacubitril+valsartan plus eplerenone both raise serum potassium (reduced aldosterone effect plus potassium excretion block); hyperkalemia risk, dangerous with renal impairment or diabetes. Management: check K+ and creatinine at 1-2 weeks and after dose changes, avoid other K-raising drugs, salt substitutes off, hold if K+ > 5.5.",
