  "Aspirin displaces valproate from protein and inhibits its clearance; free valproate rises. Management: monitor for valproate toxicity (tremor, sedation), use paracetamol instead.",
  "Carbapenems slash valproate levels 60-90% within 24-48h; seizure breakthrough. Management: avoid; if unavoidable plan alternative antiepileptic cover and expect valproate loss for days after the antibiotic stops.",
  "Valproate strongly inhibits lamotrigine glucuronidation, roughly doubling exposure; dose-dependent severe rash (SJS) risk. Management: lamotrigine dose halved and titrated slowly; stop at first sign of rash; monitor levels if available.",
