  "aceclofenac blunts telmisartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
  "aspirin blunts telmisartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
  "celecoxib blunts telmisartan effect (prostaglandin/bradykinin pathways) and can precipitate AKI in volume-depleted patients. Management: lowest NSAID dose briefly, hydrate, check creatinine and BP after NSAID start; avoid chronic NSAIDs in CKD patients on RAAS blockade.",
